don␀GMT0BST,M3.5.0/1,M10.5.0␀Paris␀CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3␀Tokyo␀JST-9␀Sydney␀AEST-10AEDT,M10.1.0,M4.1.0/3␀Los Angeles␀PST8PDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0␀Denver␀MST7MDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0␀Chicago␀CST6CDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0␀New York␀EST5EDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0␀Honolulu␀HST10␀Anchorage␀AKST9AKDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0␀Rio de Janeiro␀<-03>3␀Moscow␀MSK-3␀Dubai␀<+04>-4␀New Delhi␀IST-5:30␀Beijing␀CST-8␀UTC␀UTC0␀Copies this board's firmware onto another Heltec V4 by wire. Your settings, Wi-Fi password␀and files are NOT copied: the other board starts fresh, at the boot menu.␀  This board  GPIO 43 (TX)  ->  RX  (GPIO 44)  other V4␀  This board  GPIO 44 (RX)  <-  TX  (GPIO 43)  other V4␀  This board  GND           --  GND             other V4␀  Optional:   GPIO 3 -> RST,  GPIO 33 -> GPIO 0 (PRG)   (then it resets by itself)␀Power the other board from its own USB-C. Without the optional wires: on the other board␀hold PRG, tap RST, let go of PRG, then press Start.␀How it's worked out: power at the antenna / the antenna's effective area (G x wavelength^2 / 4 pi) = power density.␀Limits (FCC 47 CFR 1.1310, at 915 MHz): 0.61 mW/cm^2 general public, 3.05 mW/cm^2 occupational, averaged 30 min.␀It's an estimate, good to a few dB: antenna gain, the board's front-end and reflections all move it. The receiver␀tops out near 0 dBm, so right beside a meter it reads LOW (you'll see OVERLOAD). For a signed-off number use a␀calibrated broadband RF exposure meter. Meters and their ICMs are FCC-certified to meet these limits at 20 cm.␀ffaa5500␀ffaaaa00␀ff00aa00␀ff55ffff␀ff0000aa␀<2␀2-5␀5-10␀10-20␀20-50␀50-100␀100-250␀250+␀IP address␀MAC address␀Ping (ms)␀Maker / note␀ESP32 board␀Apple␀Amazon␀Google␀Roku␀Microsoft VM␀TP-Link␀Synology␀Withings␀Nest␀Pencil␀Brush␀Eraser␀Spray␀Line␀Box␀Filled box␀Oval␀Filled oval␀Paint fill␀Wireless mesh␀Status light␀GPS module␀power on␀external pin␀crash␀crash (interrupt)␀crash (task)␀watchdog␀deep sleep␀low voltage (brownout)␀SDIO␀Running␀Ready␀Waiting␀Paused␀Ending␀Performance␀Apps␀Tasks␀Stor